# Vendored rade_c (RADE V1 + V2 pure-C)

Source: https://github.com/freedv/rade_c @ 262a980842e1bc8008249d53421aca0c03bf276f
(merge of PR #20, dr-tx-bpf).

Copied verbatim from rade_c/src: the library sources listed in sources.mk
(everything the upstream `rade` library target builds) plus their headers.
CLI tools, tests and CMake are not vendored.

Like upstream, it builds against Opus's patched DNN code (nnet core,
config.h, opus_types.h, ...): here the subset in vendor/opus_dnn, which also
provides the LPCNet feature extractor and FARGAN vocoder the daemon uses for
speech <-> features.

One daemon-local change, to be proposed upstream: a V2 latent hook
(rade_set_latent_hook in rade_api.h; latent_hook in rade_tx_v2_state and
rade_rx_v2_state), a callback on each modem frame's latent vector between the
encoder and the OFDM modulator, and between the demodulator and frame sync.
dsp/rade_voice.c uses it for keyed voice scrambling. Re-apply it on update.

API: single unified `rade_api.h`; select V2 with rade_open(model, RADE_MODE_V2 | flags).

To update: re-copy the same files from a newer rade_c checkout, update the
commit above, and run `make -C vendor/rade_c` plus the daemon build.

Standalone sanity build (rade_c + vendor/opus_dnn):

    make -C vendor/rade_c
